For the proof it is enough to show that there exists a sequence $K \xrightarrow {u} L \to M \to 0$ where $K$ and $L$ are $I$-adically complete $A$-modules. This can be shown by choosing a presentation $F_1 \to F_0 \to M \to 0$ with $F_ i$ free and then setting $K$ and $L$ equal to the $f$-adic completions of $F_1$ and $F_0$. Namely, as $f$ is a nonzerodivisor these completions will be the derived completions and the sequence will remain exact.